{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQ8CkFpVarSTCZ96BPtT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Airbnb's take rate went up each year from FY2022 to FY2024:\n\n- **FY2022:** 13.3% (revenue $8,399M ÷ gross booking value $63,212M)\n- **FY2023:** 13.5% (revenue $9,917M ÷ gross booking value $73,252M)\n- **FY2024:** 13.6% (revenue $11,102M ÷ gross booking value $81,784M)\n\n**Trend:** It rose by about 25 basis points in 2023 and then held at about 13.5–13.6% in 2024, as revenue grew at roughly the same 12% pace as gross booking value.\n\nI worked out the rates from the figures in Airbnb's filings; Airbnb doesn't report them itself. Gross booking value is the total value of bookings, including host earnings, service fees, cleaning fees and taxes, so the take rate isn't a pure commission rate.\n\n**Sources**\n- Form 10-K for FY2024, filed 2025-02-13, accession 0001559720-25-000010: gross booking value for 2023–2024 and revenue for 2022–2024 (XBRL)\n- Form 10-K for FY2023, filed 2024-02-16, accession 0001559720-24-000006: gross booking value for 2022 and revenue for 2022–2023 (XBRL)\n- Form 10-K for FY2022, filed 2023-02-17, accession 0001559720-23-000003: revenue for 2022 (XBRL)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":554,"cache_read_input_tokens":11711,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":554},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4d7460b2-3d0e-4193-b955-32cd8d9f89ce","uuid":"7906aefc-797d-4c2f-b018-8f8105fa9475","timestamp":"2026-10-26T03:18:06.768Z","request_id":"req_011CgQ8CjzwZmP4wVGMcwU6Y"}
